          "source_text_sha256": "5a39723a23408652fde28ceadb686d72266fdabed75c4725634b5b37517001ac",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Recent testimony (14/01/2015) of an old observation. On February 3, 2012, at 6:04 PM, a witness observed in the sky a luminous, oblong phenomenon, slowly and silently following a straight trajectory. The object disappeared after a few minutes. The observation lasted 2 minutes during which the witness took the time to take pictures. No other testimony was collected. The witness observed from the North/Northwest a very bright, oblong yellow shape moving slowly in a straight line. The sun had been set for approximately 30 minutes. This phenomenon corresponds very well to a condensation trail of a distant plane (>50 km) illuminated by the setting sun. A clear sky is enough to observe this type of phenomenon in the half-hour following sunset (or before sunrise). See an explanation of \"strange aircraft trails\" on page 3 of the news on the website www.cnes-geipan.fr. The GEIPAN classifies this case as B: probable observation of an aircraft trail.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "de6420f2c7cb020d19996b3aecb010270facfc3c336e2e44d568bc1b548500f4"
        }
